<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Dmitrievich of Pereslavl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1302</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Dmitrievich was the last prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pereslavl-zalessky">Pereslavl-Zalessky</a>, a son of Grand Prince Dmitry of Vladimir and grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a>. He died childless in 1302 and bequeathed his principality to his uncle Daniel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. The bequest, contested by the grand princes of Vladimir, became an early step in the territorial growth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a>.</p></div>
